menu "IPRO6S A2DP sink example"

config BT_DEVICE_NAME
    string "Bluetooth device name"
    default "IPRO6S-Speaker"
    help
      Name a phone or computer shows when it searches for Bluetooth devices.

config BT_COD
    hex "Class of Device"
    default 0x240414
    help
      Class of Device sent in inquiry responses. 0x240414 is
      Audio/Video - Loudspeaker with the Audio and Rendering service bits,
      so phones list the board as a speaker.

config APP_I2S_OUTPUT
    bool "Play decoded audio on I2S"
    default y
    help
      Decode SBC and send 16-bit PCM to the I2S port (master, standard
      I2S, 16-bit slots) for an external I2S DAC or amplifier. Without it
      the app still receives and decodes the stream and reports it.

config APP_I2S_PIN_BASE
    int "First GPIO of the I2S group"
    default 0
    depends on APP_I2S_OUTPUT
    help
      The I2S signals follow the GPIO number modulo 4: BCLK on base,
      FS on base + 1, DO on base + 3. base must be a multiple of 4.
      0 puts them on the EVK's H1 header (GPIO0, GPIO1, GPIO3).

endmenu
